<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<div style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif" style="">Dear {!Lead.OwnerFirstName},&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">The lead&nbsp; {!Lead.Name} from {!Lead.Company}&nbsp;</font>owned by you has been in Lead Stage “SAL”, and the Lead Status has not been changed to “Qualified,” “Disqualified,” “Unreachable,” or “Passed to Partner” within the maximum SLA time.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif">&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif">Click&nbsp;<a href="{!Lead.Link}">here</a><a href="https://intel.my.salesforce.com//p/email/template/EmailTemplateEditorUi/{!Lead.Link}" style="">&nbsp;</a>to visit this lead record in SFDC</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><div style=""><font face="Arial, sans-serif">As a reminder, the following SLA’s are expected for any SAL lead:&nbsp;</font></div><div style=""><font face="Arial, sans-serif">&nbsp;</font></div><div style=""><font face="Arial, sans-serif">&nbsp; &nbsp; - Initial Task (Email or Phone Call) to be logged within 1 business day of acceptance&nbsp;</font></div><div style=""><font face="Arial, sans-serif">&nbsp; &nbsp; - Qualification or Rejection via Lead Status to occur within 4 business weeks of acceptance&nbsp;</font></div><div style=""><font face="Arial, sans-serif">Please disposition the record by reaching out to the lead ASAP and mark with the appropriate Lead Status. Please be sure to log all emails or called.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</font></div></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="Arial, sans-serif" style="">Thank you, please refer to <a href="https://salescrm.intel.com/training-and-help/lead-management/">this document</a> if you have questions regarding how to manage any lead assigned to you or claimed by you.</font></div></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>